  "portal_description": "Red Hat Satellite is a systems management tool for Linux-based infrastructures. It allows for provisioning, remote management and monitoring of multiple Linux deployments with a single, centralized tool. It performs provisioning and configuration management of predefined standard operating environments.\n\nThis update provides a set of base packages for the Satellite server and capsule. For the full list of new features provided by Satellite 6.2 see the Release Notes linked to in the references section. Please see the Satellite 6 Installation Guide for detailed instructions on how to install or upgrade from prior versions of Satellite 6.\n\nAll users who require Satellite version 6.2 are advised to install these new packages.\n\nChanges to the Configuration Management component:\n\n* As part of upgrading to the latest Puppet 3.x version, the hiera package has now been updated to 1.3. (BZ#1297834)\n\n* Red Hat Satellite 6.2 upgrades to the 3.8 stream of puppet. (BZ#1217527)\n\nChanges to the Performance component:\n\n* Extraneous progress tracking was slowing package installation via Satellite 6.1. This tracking has been removed, and performance is much improved. (BZ#1277292)\n\nChanges to the Users & Roles component:\n\n* With this release, a \"Test Connection\" button was added to verify LDAP connection information. (BZ#1144232)\n\n* Satellite 6.2 provides improvements to the integration of Active Directory. (BZ#1315258)",
